# Workspace

## Directory Map

| Directory | Purpose | What goes here |
|-----------|---------|---------------|
| `INBOX/` | Landing zone | Unsorted items, screenshots, bookmarks, new research dumps — **and plans**. Temporary and gitignored; nothing here is version-controlled. |
| `PROJECTS/` | Where work happens | Everything you have multiple sessions about — code, job search, relocation, finances, health plans, writing projects. If you're working on it, it's a project. |
| `RESOURCES/` | Reference material | Research about things *outside* this workspace — deep dives, technical references, templates. Pure knowledge, indexed for retrieval. |
| `ARTIFACTS/` | Records of work you did | Investigations, measurements, benchmark data, published artifacts, plans that ran. Tracked and committed. Organised per piece of work, not flat. |
| `.multiplai/memory/` | Claude's context about you | Profile, preferences, career history. Managed by the `multiplai-context` plugin; also reachable via the `dotfiles/memory/` symlink. See `.multiplai/memory/CLAUDE.md` for the index. |
| `.multiplai/diary/` | Session diary | Auto-generated per-day session logs (`YYYY-MM-DD.md`). Don't edit directly. |
| `.multiplai/learnings/` | Pending learnings | Auto-captured on session stop. Consolidate via `/multiplai-context:dream-remember`. |

## Routing Rules

When creating or saving files, put them in the right place:

| Content type | Goes to | Example |
|-------------|---------|---------|
| Research about something external | `RESOURCES/` | `RESOURCES/topic-name-YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| A record of work you did here | `ARTIFACTS/` | `ARTIFACTS/{investigation}/measurements.md` |
| **Any published Artifact** | `ARTIFACTS/` | The source `.html`/`.md` behind an Artifact URL — see below |
| Plans and recommendations | `INBOX/` | `INBOX/plan-{name}-YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| New unsorted items | `INBOX/` | Screenshots, links, raw notes |
| Memory updates | `.multiplai/memory/` | Update existing files, don't create new ones without asking |

**`RESOURCES/` vs `ARTIFACTS/`** — the line is who produced the subject matter.
Research about something external is `RESOURCES/`. A record of work done here —
what was measured, what was tried, what the numbers were — is `ARTIFACTS/`.

**Plans stay in `INBOX/` and are disposable by design.** A plan is scaffolding:
it either materialises into work or it goes stale. It is not promoted when the
work finishes — the *record of the work* is, to `ARTIFACTS/`.

**Published Artifacts go straight to `ARTIFACTS/`, never `INBOX/`.** When Claude
writes a file to publish with the Artifact tool, that file is the source of a URL
someone may hold for months. `INBOX/` is gitignored, so a file there is one
cleanup away from a live URL with no recoverable source. Write it to
`ARTIFACTS/{name}.html` and publish from there, so re-publishing to the same URL
later is still possible.

## Project Registry

Add your projects here as you create them. A project is anything you work on across multiple sessions — code, life tasks, planning, creative work. Creating a directory in `PROJECTS/` is how you tell the system "this is a thing I'm working on." It anchors files, session context, and learnings to a coherent thread.

Projects can be temporary (delete when done — diary and learnings persist regardless) or long-running. Code projects often have their own git repo; non-code projects are tracked by the workspace repo.

| Project | Own Git | Own Venv | Description |
|---------|---------|----------|-------------|
| | | | |

**Examples of project types:**
- Code: `PROJECTS/my-app/` — has its own git, venv, CI
- Job search: `PROJECTS/jobs/` — applications, resumes, interview notes
- Life admin: `PROJECTS/relocation/` — visa docs, apartment hunting, checklists
- Health: `PROJECTS/fitness/` — exercise plans, tracking, meal prep
- Writing: `PROJECTS/blog/` — drafts, briefs, published posts
- Financial: `PROJECTS/taxes/` — tax prep, receipts, filing notes

### Venv Rules

If a sub-project has its own venv, ALWAYS use `--directory`:
```
uv run --directory PROJECTS/<name> pytest tests/
```

### Git Rules

- **Projects with own `.git/`:** Commit inside that project directory.
- **Everything else:** Tracked by the workspace root git repo.
